  "method": {
    "form_wall": "Median of three complete subprocess wall times, each divided by its six batches times the number of independent expressions per batch. Includes amortized startup, parsing, input preparation, trace4, sort, term-count printing, dropping outputs and process teardown. No scalar projection or correctness verification.",
    "form_cpu": "FORM TIMER_ around trace4 plus .sort only, after sorting input expressions. Millisecond batch resolution; median of last five of six batches per process, then median of three processes. Reported separately from wall time.",
    "idenso": "Median of five per-call wall times obtained by timing loops over warm simplify_gamma calls. Inputs, initialization, and validation excluded. Result destruction included.",
    "phases": "Isolated copy of the current kernel, compiled opt-level=2 against the exact same optimized dependency artifacts. Products collected into a Vec before add_many to separately time metric construction, product materialization (coefficient/metric copies and mul_many), and add_many sum canonicalization. These phase measurements are diagnostic and include small instrumentation/materialization changes; direct kernel and full API totals agree closely.",
    "correctness": "The copied kernel result is asserted exactly equal to the production result on each test input. This is only a profiling integrity check, not an independent algebraic correctness test. FORM term counts are recorded separately.",
    "comparison": "Use FORM amortized wall time for ratios; internal CPU times are supporting diagnostics. Batch mode holds more simultaneous expressions than the Idenso call loop. This measures this free-index benchmark, not general FORM parity."
